An activity for teaching simple linear regression

1.	Go to “Canvas > Files > Datasets> Group datasets” and download your group’s dataset.
2.	Load into RStudio. Hint: Use read.csv() function
3.	Inspect the data. Identify the independent variable (first column) and dependent variable (second column). Which one is X? Y?
4.	Discuss your prior regarding the relationship Y=f(X). What is the “mechanism”?
5.	Summarize the data. Hint: use the skim() function, which you load using library(skimr).
6.	Plot the data in a scatterplot. Hint: you will need library(tidyverse) and use ggplot()+geom_point().
7.	Estimate and store the model. Hint: model<-lm(formula=    , data =       )
8.	Summarize the model. Hint: summary(model)
9.	Identify the model coefficients and R^2 value. Interpret each. How do they conform to your prior from step 4? 
10.	Use your estimated model to make one prediction.
